WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.910
 If you want to lead
something, start by saying,

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:04.320
this is what I care about.

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:05.970
This is what I
want to do and why

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:10.850
I think you should care about
it and you should want to help.

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:12.950
Hardly a day goes
by that I don't

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:15.030
think how fast my
life has flown,

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:17.330
how I remember as if it were
yesterday the first day I

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:18.627
became president.

00:00:18.627 --> 00:00:23.200
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:26.590
 Hardly anything worth
doing can be done alone.

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:30.852
This is a particularly
disorienting time for billions

00:00:30.852 --> 00:00:31.810
of people in the world.

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:34.480
You've got major
uncertainties about what's

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.670
going to happen in
the years ahead.

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:39.790
At a time like that, you really
need good leadership skills.

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:42.010
And you need people
whose goal it

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:45.940
is to pull people together,
not drive them apart.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:48.280
People need to
feel the potential

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:50.658
to create a better tomorrow.

00:00:50.658 --> 00:00:52.700
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.190
 This class is unlike
anything I've ever done.

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:57.980
I'll be teaching skills
I developed and used

00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:00.990
in very challenging
leadership positions.

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:03.860
And I hope that those
skills will help you

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:06.560
in your personal and
professional lives.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:08.240
You'll learn how
to work with people

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:11.570
you don't agree with,
may not even like,

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:14.270
and how to mediate conflicts.

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:17.450
I don't believe being nice
is inconsistent with being

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:18.630
tough and smart.

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:23.420
You've got to be tough as
nails with your tender heart.

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:25.370
I have encountered
a lot of setbacks.

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:28.100
I lost two elections
after I entered politics.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:31.100
I've had ferocious
opposition, where

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:34.430
the whole strategy was to try
to destroy me as a person.

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:38.890
My mother died after
I became president.

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:41.950
I've had a lot of
things that really hurt.

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:44.050
But in the end, the
great adventure of life

00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:46.570
is what you decide
to do with it.

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:50.140
We're all struggling mortals
with fleeting lives who

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:52.580
are trying to be right
as often as we can

00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:55.240
and trying to live a life
that amounts to something.

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:57.010
A good leader will
share the credit

00:01:57.010 --> 00:01:59.830
when something good happens
and assume responsibility

00:01:59.830 --> 00:02:02.500
for the mistakes and not
look for a scapegoat.

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:04.780
I believe leaders
are not just born.

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:06.070
They are also made.

00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:09.130
And I hope everybody who watches
this will say, what am I going

00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:12.880
to do to be a better leader?

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:17.350
I'm President Bill Clinton,
and this is MasterClass.

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:20.400
[MUSIC PLAYING]

